[{:db/id "c0c5a825-f639-5ea1-9df7-8def67861623" :answer/id #uuid "c0c5a825-f639-5ea1-9df7-8def67861623" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{122 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{9}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4a95c0e4-a164-5d09-9222-9c149c45ab7d" :answer/id #uuid "4a95c0e4-a164-5d09-9222-9c149c45ab7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{122 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ddb39b70-4ea5-52bd-a660-df7df68c411f" :answer/id #uuid "ddb39b70-4ea5-52bd-a660-df7df68c411f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{122 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{9}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6e41dde2-dfa2-5092-b54e-8a8248dcf4a1" :answer/id #uuid "6e41dde2-dfa2-5092-b54e-8a8248dcf4a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{123 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4498327b-6560-51a2-b3e5-e74c8480729b" :answer/id #uuid "4498327b-6560-51a2-b3e5-e74c8480729b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "74e20894-f26f-5e9b-8de6-fcc616806ae9" :answer-field/id #uuid "74e20894-f26f-5e9b-8de6-fcc616806ae9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c0c5a825-f639-5ea1-9df7-8def67861623" "4a95c0e4-a164-5d09-9222-9c149c45ab7d" "ddb39b70-4ea5-52bd-a660-df7df68c411f" "6e41dde2-dfa2-5092-b54e-8a8248dcf4a1" "4498327b-6560-51a2-b3e5-e74c8480729b"] :answer-field/correct "c0c5a825-f639-5ea1-9df7-8def67861623" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4ddd94b2-cc71-504e-a7a5-1df422f9b408" :question/id #uuid "4ddd94b2-cc71-504e-a7a5-1df422f9b408" :question/problem "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4{x}^{2},\\,4\\le xy\\le 5\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,4\\le v\\le 5\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} & \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{5}{v}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{5}{v}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{4}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{5}{v}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{5}{v}^{2}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}\\,{|}_{4}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{9}\\cdot (125-64) \\\\  & =\\frac{122\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["74e20894-f26f-5e9b-8de6-fcc616806ae9"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d44bf487-a72f-5688-b79f-679c5c9843de" :answer/id #uuid "d44bf487-a72f-5688-b79f-679c5c9843de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "85 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7ea0e4fa-607a-52bf-a6d1-09e1f76b57f0" :answer/id #uuid "7ea0e4fa-607a-52bf-a6d1-09e1f76b57f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1760086a-7c09-5e8c-b8a1-c75d9fe9a51b" :answer/id #uuid "1760086a-7c09-5e8c-b8a1-c75d9fe9a51b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cf2b0b28-1110-5655-97fd-3599b3b30adf" :answer/id #uuid "cf2b0b28-1110-5655-97fd-3599b3b30adf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6a996faf-b917-5a49-b738-11415367209b" :answer/id #uuid "6a996faf-b917-5a49-b738-11415367209b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 28 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e0c9be7b-466c-5bfe-beef-e661d5145178" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0c9be7b-466c-5bfe-beef-e661d5145178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d44bf487-a72f-5688-b79f-679c5c9843de" "7ea0e4fa-607a-52bf-a6d1-09e1f76b57f0" "1760086a-7c09-5e8c-b8a1-c75d9fe9a51b" "cf2b0b28-1110-5655-97fd-3599b3b30adf" "6a996faf-b917-5a49-b738-11415367209b"] :answer-field/correct "7ea0e4fa-607a-52bf-a6d1-09e1f76b57f0" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b880e9be-152d-5343-be07-baad51f74777" :question/id #uuid "b880e9be-152d-5343-be07-baad51f74777" :question/problem "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 16{x}^{2},\\,1\\le xy\\le 4\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 16,\\,1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} & \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{v}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{v}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{16}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{v}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡16-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{v}^{2}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{9}\\cdot (64-1) \\\\  & =14\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["e0c9be7b-466c-5bfe-beef-e661d5145178"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "719b5cba-94f5-5e18-8818-62c388bfb5f6" :answer/id #uuid "719b5cba-94f5-5e18-8818-62c388bfb5f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "088d3881-6f26-5c1e-8b70-605ffcbe6a13" :answer/id #uuid "088d3881-6f26-5c1e-8b70-605ffcbe6a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cef2c8c7-9728-5e8f-b345-f1a76f0182b0" :answer/id #uuid "cef2c8c7-9728-5e8f-b345-f1a76f0182b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "13d60485-67ff-563a-a2f9-a27075387c5f" :answer/id #uuid "13d60485-67ff-563a-a2f9-a27075387c5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{9}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4e49411c-8515-54df-bf3e-1b739c795ae9" :answer/id #uuid "4e49411c-8515-54df-bf3e-1b739c795ae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{9}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "58854fce-abbe-50be-9446-ce124d3d6e2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "58854fce-abbe-50be-9446-ce124d3d6e2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["719b5cba-94f5-5e18-8818-62c388bfb5f6" "088d3881-6f26-5c1e-8b70-605ffcbe6a13" "cef2c8c7-9728-5e8f-b345-f1a76f0182b0" "13d60485-67ff-563a-a2f9-a27075387c5f" "4e49411c-8515-54df-bf3e-1b739c795ae9"] :answer-field/correct "4e49411c-8515-54df-bf3e-1b739c795ae9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a9bf5a72-2afe-55a9-8288-03e8e500cac8" :question/id #uuid "a9bf5a72-2afe-55a9-8288-03e8e500cac8" :question/problem "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 9{x}^{2},\\,2\\le xy\\le 4\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 9,\\,2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} & \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{9}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡9-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{9}\\cdot (64-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{112\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["58854fce-abbe-50be-9446-ce124d3d6e2f"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "c8511436-e484-5251-a621-0417962a64ca" :answer/id #uuid "c8511436-e484-5251-a621-0417962a64ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{182 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f7a1ff94-668d-56c9-ab15-77c13bfdd79a" :answer/id #uuid "f7a1ff94-668d-56c9-ab15-77c13bfdd79a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{182 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{9}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2c8e42dd-1135-55d6-baea-5eaf5e395812" :answer/id #uuid "2c8e42dd-1135-55d6-baea-5eaf5e395812" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{182 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{9}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5775d9e0-17da-5f4b-97d4-d8327fe13f79" :answer/id #uuid "5775d9e0-17da-5f4b-97d4-d8327fe13f79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{671 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bee804f0-fe47-54f2-82b3-1ab225bbaa16" :answer/id #uuid "bee804f0-fe47-54f2-82b3-1ab225bbaa16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2a87ecd3-6574-5e98-aac6-eaeb2a2a41af" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a87ecd3-6574-5e98-aac6-eaeb2a2a41af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c8511436-e484-5251-a621-0417962a64ca" "f7a1ff94-668d-56c9-ab15-77c13bfdd79a" "2c8e42dd-1135-55d6-baea-5eaf5e395812" "5775d9e0-17da-5f4b-97d4-d8327fe13f79" "bee804f0-fe47-54f2-8