eterminant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{6}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{6}{v}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{6}{v}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{4}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{6}{v}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{6}{v}^{2}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}\\,{|}_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{9}\\cdot (216-125) \\\\  & =\\frac{182\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["2a87ecd3-6574-5e98-aac6-eaeb2a2a41af"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "5ce3c7dc-caf4-59c6-bc90-66911b31b855" :answer/id #uuid "5ce3c7dc-caf4-59c6-bc90-66911b31b855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 52 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8b1f244f-0b28-5817-86a7-3ca216955106" :answer/id #uuid "8b1f244f-0b28-5817-86a7-3ca216955106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f6dbc465-6dd3-5c31-801d-8e21abfc3c96" :answer/id #uuid "f6dbc465-6dd3-5c31-801d-8e21abfc3c96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "156 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/ensure 